+
+An explicit entry in Gemini's `parts` array gives the accumulator a boundary
+that a new frame alone does not. Two text entries in one array remain two
+parts. The first entry of a later frame may continue a compatible unsigned
+part; a trailing signature may finish an unsigned text, thought, or tool part.
+Once attached, that signature closes the exact binding. Appending later text
+would change what it signed; replacing it would lose the original binding.
+Keep a standalone signature-only first part, signed text followed by unsigned
+or signed text, and signed thought followed by a separate opaque part distinct.
+Their canonical parts retain the native payload for exact-source replay.
 
